29 0 obj
<< /BS << /S /S /W 0.6>> /DA (/Helv 0 Tf 0 g) /DV () /F 4 /FT /Tx /Ff 4096 /M (D:20261102051529) /MK << /BC [0.6509803922 0.7058823529 0.7607843137] /BG [0.9843137255 0.9882352941 0.9960784314]>> /P 81 0 R /Rect [38 57.2 557.2756 203.2] /Subtype /Widget /T (project_summary) /TU (Brief project description and methodology) /Type /Annot /V (Aim: To design, implement and evaluate a market-state-conditioned orchestration\noperator that continuously varies the influence of methodologically heterogeneous\nfinancial agents over a single shared decision, and to establish, on Colombo Stock\nExchange data under a cost-aware and regime-decomposed protocol, under what\nconditions it earns its place against fixed, static learned and performance-reactive\nweighting.\n\nActivities: Design science research, with the artefact built by evolutionary\nprototyping under stage gates. A provisional set of four agents, technical,\nfundamental retrieval, volatility and liquidity, runs behind one output contract and\nfeeds an orchestrator that sets each agent's influence from measured liquidity,\nvolatility, persistence and agent confidence. Pre-trained models are used through\nthird-party APIs under their terms. Sentiment analysis is out of scope.\n\nEvaluation: Offline retrospective simulation only, with no live trading and no\ndeployment. Five weighting arms run over identical cached agent outputs on a rolling\nwalk-forward split of sixteen folds, with per-input ablations, cost sensitivity\nsweeps, regime decomposition and significance testing. A null result is pre-registered as reportable.\n\nData: Historical Colombo Stock Exchange price, volume, corporate action and float\nrecords, 2012 to 2026, purchased under a non-commercial student licence, plus 22,893\npublic company filings. No human participants, no personal data, nothing\nredistributed.) /AP << /N 98 0 R>>>>
endobj
